      "batch_node": {
        "source": "plugins.samsite",
        "name": "Samsite landing v0.1.8",
        "description": "Landing page: cytoscape graph projection of the samsite deployment (account 180731181784). v0.1.5 is the merge of two parallel lines onto one batch: (a) the signed /.well-known/ artifacts on the board — the seed search matches ksi_signal / vdr_report / compliance_artifact, and landing-finalize.js prunes each to the latest snapshot per kind and styles them as file cards; (b) the deploy→KEV-fetch + human-actor story — the search also matches web_host / web_document (CISA host + KEV catalog, kev-fetch.grift.json) and user (the three actors Readers / george / Sam, users.grift.json). web_host / web_document / user / the compliance file types carry no per-model tags, so they are reached by explicit per-label MATCHes (like the GitHub lane), not the Project=samsite tag scan. Fresh batch_entity_id (supersedes both 019e73fb-... and 019e73fe-...) so any session seeded from either parent re-applies the combined search; the skip-if-exists guard is batch-id-keyed. The Rekor entries collapse into a stack (tap_viz stack primitive) in landing-finalize.js. v0.1.7 adds MATCH (gapp:github_app) so the Dependabot github_app (reclassified from a workflow by the collector) renders — the finalize pass parents it to the github.com platform compound. v0.1.8 adds nav_rules to the graph panel config (interpreted generically by tap_viz graph_panel → display.tap_viz.nav_url → single-tap navigation in panel-graph.js): the signed artifacts (compliance_artifact by kind / ksi_signal / vdr_report) open their corresponding workbench viewer pages pinned by entity_id; the GitHub nodes (repository / account / platform / workflow / app) open their html_url on github.com in a new tab."
      },
      "nodes": [
        {
          "entity": {
            "entity_id": "eb9fb415-ba8d-57e5-ab3f-1e2411ce0822",
            "entity_type": "search",
            "name": "Samsite — Project=samsite nodes",
            "dimensions": {}
          },
          "node": {
            "name": "Samsite — Project=samsite nodes",
            "description": "Gryphon: aws_account + boundary + the GitHub lane (github_platform / github_account / github_repository / github_workflow, all unfiltered — they bind variables other than `n`, so the tag WHERE doesn't apply) plus a bare `MATCH (n)` typeless scan filtered to Project=samsite via the per-model tags JSONField. The GitHub source/deploy subtree carries no AWS `tags.Project`, so it's seeded by explicit per-label MATCHes rather than the tag scan. Per spec-grid-traversal-language § Envelope-Aware Field Paths, `data.tags.Project` walks the per-model tags JSONField via Django nested lookup; nodes without `data.tags` (compliance + GitHub models) gracefully don't match.",
            "search_type": "gryphon",
            "root": "node",
            "definition": {
              "query": [
                "MATCH (account:aws_account)",
                "MATCH (b:boundary)",
                "MATCH (gp:github_platform)",
                "MATCH (ga:github_account)",
                "MATCH (gr:github_repository)",
                "MATCH (gw:github_workflow)",
                "MATCH (gapp:github_app)",
                "MATCH (re:rekor_log_entry)",
                "MATCH (ca:sigstore_ca)",
                "MATCH (oi:oidc_issuer)",
                "MATCH (sig:ksi_signal)",
                "MATCH (vr:vdr_report)",
                "MATCH (cart:compliance_artifact)",
                "MATCH (wh:web_host)",
                "MATCH (wd:web_document)",
                "MATCH (u:user)",
                "MATCH (n)",
                "WHERE n.data.tags.Project = \"samsite\""
              ]
            }
          }
        },
